.TH AGENTCENTER\-CLI 1 "" "agentcenter\-cli 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
agentcenter\-cli \- AI coding sessions without the GUI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B agentcenter\-cli
<command> [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Headless AgentCenter: a snapshot of AI coding sessions as a table or JSON.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS snapshot
one sample of every AI session (table, or JSON with \-\-json)
.PP
.nf
usage: agentcenter\-cli snapshot [\-\-json] [\-\-interval\-ms N] [\-\-proc\-root PATH]

Takes two samples N ms apart and prints one row per AI session. Transcripts
are read in full on the first sample, so tokens, tool calls and the cockpit
are filled on the second (watch and the GUI read at most 1 MiB per tick).

  \-\-json            print the snapshot as JSON instead of a table
  \-\-interval\-ms N   time between the two samples (default 1000)
  \-\-proc\-root PATH  read PATH instead of /proc (fixtures)

The first line sums the agent sessions (herdr left out) by agent and by the
state the agent or its herdr pane reports (busy, blocked), and counts the
active processes: session children in state R or D or above 1 % CPU.

In the table `\-` is a missing value (no previous sample, unreadable) and a
trailing `*` marks a sum that leaves out some processes (JSON: null and
`partial`). Control characters are shown escaped (`\ex1b`, `\en`).

env AGENTCENTER_EXTRA_AGENTS=comm1,comm2 adds agents detected by comm.
.fi
.SS cockpit
what to do per agent session: context, burn, re\-read (contexto.py)
.PP
.nf
usage: agentcenter\-cli cockpit [\-\-json] [\-\-all] [\-\-timeout\-ms N] [\-\-proc\-root PATH]

One row per live agent session with the cockpit of contexto.py: what to do
(REC: CONTINUAR, COMPACTAR, HANDOFF, OCIOSA), context, weighted burn, cache
hit, re\-read share and payback, and below it the reasons (`motivo:`).
Transcripts are read in full; sampling repeats until every matched
transcript is read or the timeout runs out. On timeout what is ready is
printed, stderr says how many sessions are still reading, and the exit code
is 0. The first sample is always awaited: when it alone runs past the
timeout, the command returns right after it, without rates (interval 0).

  \-\-json            print the snapshot as JSON (same as `snapshot \-\-json`)
  \-\-all             also list idle sessions (OCIOSA), hidden by default
  \-\-timeout\-ms N    stop sampling after N ms (default 15000)
  \-\-proc\-root PATH  read PATH instead of /proc (fixtures)

Columns: CTX is context tokens / window and % (`~`: window inferred), BURN
the weighted burn and % of the session budget (CLAUDE_SESSION_BUDGET), CACHE
cache_read / tokens_in, RELEI the weighted re\-read share (it decides
HANDOFF), PBACK turns until a new session pays off, HANDOFF the age and name
of the project's last handoff, IDLE minutes since the transcript was written.

Not measured here (contexto.py does): LOOP (repeated tool calls) and files
re\-read many times. A session the script calls LOOP shows its other verdict.

The thresholds are the script's: SQUAD_CTX_PCT, SQUAD_REREAD,
SQUAD_REREAD_PISO, SQUAD_BURN_CHEIO, SQUAD_CTX_BASE, CLAUDE_SESSION_BUDGET.
env AGENTCENTER_COCKPIT_READ_BUDGET=N caps transcript bytes per tick (tests).
.fi
.SS insights
findings and a short briefing, optionally worded by a local model
.PP
.nf
usage: agentcenter\-cli insights [\-\-json] [\-\-llm URL] [\-\-llm\-timeout\-ms N]
                                [\-\-timeout\-ms N] [\-\-proc\-root PATH]

What needs attention on this machine, most urgent first: up to four findings
from fixed rules (loops, memory pressure, memory 95 % used, full contexts,
handoff due, idle memory, CPU load, sessions running 8 h or more, burn, cold
caches) and a two\-sentence briefing above them. Sessions are
sampled like `cockpit \-\-all`: transcripts are read in full, and sampling
stops after the timeout.

Without \-\-llm the briefing is the text of the rules and nothing leaves the
process. With \-\-llm a local model words the findings; its answer is checked
(length, no invented numbers, the key facts of the first finding present) and
the rule text is shown instead when the check fails, the call fails or times
out. The line `briefing: model` or `briefing: rules` says which one you read.

The model only words the findings. It never sees transcript content or
session names (the findings carry the project directory name and a pid at
most), only loopback addresses are accepted, and it is never called by
`snapshot`, `watch` or the GUI.

  \-\-json                 print { schema_version, taken_at_ms, briefing, findings }
  \-\-llm URL              OpenAI\-compatible server on loopback, e.g.
                         http://127.0.0.1:8080 (env AGENTCENTER_LLM)
  \-\-llm\-timeout\-ms N     give the model N ms in total (default 20000)
  \-\-timeout\-ms N         stop sampling after N ms (default 15000)
  \-\-proc\-root PATH       read PATH instead of /proc (fixtures)

A URL that is not http://127.0.0.1, http://localhost or http://[::1] with a
port is a usage error (exit code 2).
.fi
.SS watch
sample every second until interrupted (table, or NDJSON with \-\-json)
.PP
.nf
usage: agentcenter\-cli watch [\-\-json] [\-\-interval\-ms N] [\-\-proc\-root PATH]

Samples every N ms until interrupted and prints one snapshot per tick: the
table redrawn in place (on a terminal), or one JSON object per line (NDJSON).

  \-\-json            NDJSON: one snapshot per line, same format as `snapshot \-\-json`
  \-\-interval\-ms N   time between ticks (default 1000)
  \-\-proc\-root PATH  read PATH instead of /proc (fixtures)

The first tick has no rates (`\-`, null). PSS and swap of a session are re\-read
every 5 s if its memory moved and at most every 300 s otherwise, so they can
lag the CPU and disk columns; uid and context switches lag up to 5 s. A quiet
session (CPU under 1 %, no disk or stall) is re\-read only every 5 s: between
reads it shows the mean of its last window, and new work takes up to 5 s to
show. The agent's cmdline and cwd can be up to 5 s stale. See
`snapshot \-\-help` for the table legend.

env AGENTCENTER_EXTRA_AGENTS=comm1,comm2 adds agents detected by comm.
.fi
.SS signal
stop, resume, terminate or kill a session or one process
.PP
.nf
usage: agentcenter\-cli signal <stop|cont|term|kill> (\-\-session PID | \-\-pid PID) [\-\-yes]

Sends a signal to a whole session or to one process.

  stop   SIGSTOP, suspend (root first, so a parent cannot respawn a child)
  cont   SIGCONT, resume (leaves first)
  term   SIGTERM, ask to exit (root first)
  kill   SIGKILL, kill (root first)

  \-\-session PID  the agent PID and every process of its session
  \-\-pid PID      only this process
  \-\-yes          do not ask; without it the processes are listed and a
                 terminal is asked to confirm (no terminal: nothing is sent)

Only processes of your own user are signalled, never this process, its
ancestors, pid 1 or the herdr server. Each pid is checked again right before
its signal; a pid reused by another process is skipped.

env AGENTCENTER_EXTRA_AGENTS=comm1,comm2 adds agents detected by comm.
.fi
.SS reclaim
idle sessions by memory, with the command to end each (read only)
.PP
.nf
usage: agentcenter\-cli reclaim [\-\-json] [\-\-window\-s N] [\-\-proc\-root PATH]

Watches every AI session for N seconds (one sample per second) and lists the
idle ones, largest PSS + SwapPss first, with the memory they would free and
the command that would end each one. Read only: nothing is signalled.

  \-\-json            print {window_s, total_bytes, sessions[]} as JSON
  \-\-window\-s N      seconds to watch (default 10, at least 1)
  \-\-proc\-root PATH  read PATH instead of /proc (fixtures)

A session is idle when its overlay status is `idle` (Claude, herdr), or, when
no overlay gives a status, when its CPU stayed under 1% of a core in every
sample of the window. A session that was not seen with a complete CPU sum in
every sample (new, or a new process in it) is not idle. `busy` and `blocked`
sessions are never listed. Also left out: the multiplexer (herdr server), the
session this command runs in, and sessions whose PSS cannot be read (another
user's). A quiet session is re\-read every 5 s, so its CPU is the mean of the
last 5 s. In the table `*` marks a memory sum that leaves out some processes.

env AGENTCENTER_EXTRA_AGENTS=comm1,comm2 adds agents detected by comm.
.fi
